{"id":"u-6cdbaae7-6274-45b1-860e-8e954293722a","src":"community","title":"The Aesthetic Density-12-Week Hypertrophy","author":"LOST ARC primes","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/uZfXq9-12-week-hypertrophy-and-joint-safety-plan","desc":"The purpose is to facilitate a complete body recomposition for individuals with a lean starting point. It is designed to bridge the gap between a standard \"fit\" look and the high-density, \"3D\" muscularity seen in AI-generated physiques. The program utilizes scientific volume allocation and eccentric control (3S Lowering) to maximize muscle fiber recruitment while prioritizing joint longevity and systemic safety.\n\nThe program follows a \"Specialization Split\" logic. While it maintains the foundational strength of the whole body, it over-allocates weekly sets to specific \"Aesthetic Pillars\":\n\n3-PHASE PROGRESSION\nPhase 1: Foundation (Weeks 1-4)\n\nFocus: Tempo Mastery & Joint Prep.\n\nVolume: 90–100 weekly sets, RPE 7-8.\n\nPriority: Mastering the 3S Lowering phase on all priority lifts.\n\nPhase 2: Intensification (Weeks 5-8)\n\nFocus: Progressive Overload & Weight Increase.\n\nVolume: 110–120 weekly sets, RPE 8-9.\n\nTechniques: Added Cable Tension, Load Scaling (+2.5kg bi-weekly).\n\nPhase 3: Peak Specialization (Weeks 9-12)\n\nFocus: Maximum Hypertrophy & Density.\n\nVolume: 130–150 weekly sets, RPE 9-10.\n\nNote: Includes a mandatory Deload in Week 9 to allow for systemic recovery before the final 3-week peak.\n\nPRIORITY MUSCLE TARGETING (Weekly Sets)\nARMS (3x/week stimulus): 22 sets total.\n\nDELTS (2x/week stimulus): 18 sets total.\n\nCORE (3x/week stimulus): 18 sets total.\n\nCHEST (2x/week stimulus): 15 sets total.\n\nCALVES (2x/week stimulus): 12 sets total (High intensity).","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-06T16:40:11.509Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Shoulder & Arm Priority","Legs & Bicep Frequency","Upper Chest & Back (Volume Day","Hamstring & Delt Refinement"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":6,"x":4}],"note":"7kg\nLight weight- 3s lowering phase)"},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"14Kg - Neutral Seated"},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Weight: 10kg DBs\n(Safe for elbow)"},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"ROPE \nWeight: 17.5kg (Focus on the flare)"},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"r":20,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Sets/Reps: 3 x Max | RPE 9"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Weight: 22kg DB"},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Choose your weight t hit 15 reps"},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Standing - 10kg DBs"},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":10,"x":4}],"note":"Sets/Reps: 5 x 15 | RPE 10 (Full stretch)"},{"n":"Leg Raise (Captain's Chair)","sets":[{"r":20,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":3}],"note":"Low Incline DB Press (30°)\n16kg DBs (Based on 20kg Max to ensure 10 clean reps)"},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Starting weight 35kg - Focus on 3S lowering to build chest density"},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":4}],"note":"Neutral Grip"},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"45kg (Focus on squeeze, not momentum)"},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":20,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Face Pulls: 10kg – 12.5kg (Cable Stack).\nDo not go too heavy. Use a weight where you can pull the rope toward your forehead and hold it for 1 second without your body swinging."}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Weight: 40kg - USE STRAPS"},{"n":"One Arm Lateral Raise (Cable)",